<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is MCP?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">The Model Context Protocol is an open standard that lets AI agents connect to tools and data, such as a calendar, a database or a cloud account, through one common interface.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is the new MCP specification more secure?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">It removes some older risks, including protocol-managed sessions and weak OAuth grants, but Akamai researchers also identified new attack surfaces because responsibility for verifying state moved to implementers.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is the OWASP MCP Top 10?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">An OWASP project listing the ten most likely ways to compromise an MCP deployment. It is in beta and labelled with the 2025 edition, so use it as a question sheet and expect changes.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What should I ask an agent supplier first?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Three things: what permissions the agent has and who reviews them, where its credentials are stored and how often they rotate, and whether you can see a log of everything it did last week.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

